397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 764 0 R
/E (Radial Symmetry: All cases showed consistent circular spreading, confirming isotropic diffusion and a level experimental setup.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 765 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 766 0 R
/E (Viscosity Inhibition: The addition of Glycerol drastically slowed expansion. This validates the Stokes-Einstein relation, showing that fluid resistance is a dominant factor in mass transfer.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 767 0 R
/E (Unsteady-State Behavior: Peak concentration at the center decayed over time as the dye redistributed. This "fading" confirms the point-source analytical model.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 768 0 R
/E (Linearity \(r^2 vs. time\): The linear relationship between squared radius and time across all samples confirms that the transport mechanism was fundamentally Fickian Diffusion)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 239 0 R
/E (Sources of Error)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 769 0 R
/E (Parallax & Camera Alignment: If the camera wasn't perfectly perpendicular to the petri dish, circular dye spreads would appear as ellipses, skewing the radial \(r\) measurements.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 770 0 R
/E (Initial Momentum: The force of the pipette drop creates a "splash" or mechanical push, causing faster initial spreading that isn't true molecular diffusion.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 771 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 772 0 R
/E (Density Currents: KMnO4 is denser than water. The dye "slumps" and spreads across the bottom of the dish due to gravity, leading to higher "apparent" D values.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 773 0 R
/E (Optical Saturation: The camera sensor cannot distinguish between "very dark" and "pitch black." This makes the center of the drop appear wider and flatter \(the plateau effect\) than it physically is.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 774 0 R
/E (Vibrations: Any movement of the table or floor during the 25-minute runs could induce minor mixing, artificially increasing the spreading rate.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 775 0 R
/E (Glycerol Mixing: If the Glycerol and water weren't 100% homogenized, the dye might have hit "pockets" of different viscosities, causing uneven spreading.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 240 0 R
/E (Experimental Precautions)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 776 0 R
/E (Level Surface: Ensure the petri dish is on a perfectly horizontal surface to prevent gravity-driven flow from biasing the dye spread in one direction.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
412 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 777 0 R
/E (Thermal Equilibrium: Allow the water/glycerol mix to reach a stable temperature before injecting the dye to avoid unintended internal convection currents.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 778 0 R
/E (Minimal Drop Height: Use a micropipette to release the dye as close to the water surface as possible to prevent "splashing" or initial momentum errors.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
414 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 779 0 R
/E (Zero Vibration: Keep the experimental bench isolated from movements, foot traffic, or loud sounds that could induce mechanical mixing during the long 25-minute runs.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
415 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 780 0 R
/E (Ambient Lighting: Maintain constant, diffuse lighting to prevent glare on the water surface, which can cause errors in the image processing software.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
416 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 781 0 R
/E (Pure Reagents: Use distilled water to ensure no impurities or ions interfere with the KMnO4 diffusion kinetics.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 782 0 R
/E (Cover the Dish: Use a transparent lid or cover to prevent evaporation and air currents from disturbing the water surface during long-duration observations.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
